# TransferIQ backend settings: sample file.
#
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env      (backend/.env is gitignored: real values go there, never in this file)
#
# As copied, this file runs the app OFFLINE in demo mode: offline matcher, in-memory data reset on restart, role
# switcher in the top bar, no Azure account needed. Uncomment a group below to switch that service on.
#
# The app does not read .env by itself. Load it into the environment before starting uvicorn:
#   bash:        set -a; source .env; set +a; uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000
#   PowerShell:  see "Run" in .claude/skills/run-transferiq/SKILL.md
# Tests always run offline, whatever is in .env.
#
# Leave optional settings commented out rather than empty: an empty value is not the same as "unset" for some
# of them (e.g. an empty TRANSFERIQ_AUTH_MODE is not demo mode, an empty TRANSFERIQ_DEMO_PASSWORD is an empty password).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- sign-in
# demo   = role switcher, for local development (default)
# portal = TransferIQ accounts with sign-in and Register (what the live demo uses)
# entra  = Microsoft Entra ID single sign-on with app roles (infra/README.md)
TRANSFERIQ_AUTH_MODE=demo
# TRANSFERIQ_DEMO_PASSWORD=admin                 # password of the seeded sample accounts (portal mode)
# TRANSFERIQ_SESSION_SECRET=<random 64 hex>      # signs portal sessions; unset = random per start (everyone signed out on restart)
# TRANSFERIQ_CHAT_SECRET=<random 64 hex>         # signs public chat turns (>= 32 chars); set it outside demo mode, else chat context is lost on restart
# ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<tenant GUID>                  # entra mode only
# ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=<API app registration GUID>    # entra mode only
# TRANSFERIQ_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200  # comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Azure OpenAI (matcher + chat)
# Without AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT the matcher uses its offline engine (ADR 0003) and the UI shows "offline-fallback".
# Foundry portal -> project -> Models + endpoints -> the deployment:
#   endpoint   = the "Target URI" up to and including .com (not the .../api/projects/... project endpoint)
#   deployment = the deployment name; a gpt-4o / gpt-4.1 family model (o-series and gpt-5 reject temperature 0)
# In Azure the app signs in with its managed identity; the key is only a local-development fallback.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-mini
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=<key, local development only>
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-06-01
# TRANSFERIQ_PREWARM=1                           # 0 = skip the warm-up model call at start-up

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- Azure AI Search (BU course shortlist)
# AZURE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://<service>.search.windows.net
# AZURE_SEARCH_INDEX=bu-courses
# AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY=<key, local development only>
# AZURE_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT=<embedding deployment, e.g. text-embedding-3-small>   # optional: adds vector search
# AZURE_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=               # defaults to AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT
# AZURE_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=                # defaults to the managed identity / AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY

# ------------------------------------------------------- Azure AI Document Intelligence (OCR for scanned PDFs)
# Text PDFs are read locally; this is only needed for scanned transcripts.
# AZURE_DI_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.cognitiveservices.azure.com
# AZURE_DI_KEY=<key, local development only>
# TRANSFERIQ_PDF_TIMEOUT_S=15                    # max seconds to read one uploaded PDF

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- PostgreSQL
# Without POSTGRES_HOST, data is kept in memory and reset to the seed data on restart.
# Without POSTGRES_PASSWORD the app signs in with an Entra token for its managed identity.
# POSTGRES_HOST=<server>.postgres.database.azure.com
# POSTGRES_DB=butransfer
# POSTGRES_USER=<user>
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<password, local development only>
# POSTGRES_SCHEMA=public

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- Blob Storage (uploaded PDFs, accounts)
# AZURE_STORAGE_BLOB_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Email: syllabus requests
# First configured wins: Communication Services, then the Logic App webhook. Without either, requests are
# recorded and shown in the app, but no email is sent.
# AZURE_COMMUNICATION_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.communication.azure.com
# ACS_SENDER_ADDRESS=DoNotReply@<domain>
# NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=<Logic App HTTP trigger URL; it contains its own access signature, keep it secret>
# SYLLABUS_REQUEST_TO=credit-office@example.edu  # comma-separated
# SYLLABUS_REQUEST_CC=
# APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4200             # base of the upload link in the email
# TRANSFERIQ_SYLLABUS_REMINDER_DAYS=2            # remind every N days until the syllabus arrives; 0 = no reminders
# TRANSFERIQ_SYLLABUS_REMINDER_MAX=7
# TRANSFERIQ_SYLLABUS_REMINDER_CHECK_MINUTES=60

# --------------------------------------------------------------- public credit check and chat (no sign-in)
# TRANSFERIQ_PUBLIC_PER_MIN=20                   # requests per minute per IP
# TRANSFERIQ_PUBLIC_AI_PER_IP_HOUR=40            # AI chat turns per hour per IP
# TRANSFERIQ_PUBLIC_AI_PER_HOUR=300              # AI chat turns per hour in total
# TRANSFERIQ_PUBLIC_CHAT_CONCURRENCY=4

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- data
# TRANSFERIQ_SEED_DIR=../data/synthetic/seed     # default: data/synthetic/seed in the repo
